# Check out text files with LF line endings on every machine.
# Knowledge sources are fingerprinted (sha256 in knowledge/registry.json): a Windows
# checkout that converted them to CRLF would change the bytes, and the pilot would then
# refuse calls. Python, PowerShell and the docs all work fine with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.docx binary
*.zip  binary
